ommunity examples that carry the idea before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Example simplified flow: idea → bill → debate → vote → law (details vary by level). Road rules are laws enforced by poli Then write your own evidence.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which source or place detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Example simplified flow: idea → bill → debate → vote → law (details vary by level). Road rules are laws enforced by poli Then write your own evidence."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Make the HSIE idea visible: name the observation, source or example you used and say why it supports the claim. Supported records follow the actual sources and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["An answer copied without understanding","Make the HSIE idea visible: name the observation, source or example you used and say why it supports the claim","A guess with no evidence","A claim unrelated to the source or place"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about law with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample simplified flow: idea → bill → debate → vote → law (details vary by level). Road rules are laws enforced by police. Look at each observation, source detail or example that carries the idea.\n\nTRY FIRST\nList the key observations, sources or steps from the model and say what each one shows.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful record names the evidence and the reason it supports the claim, not only a label.","explain":"